Overlayfs: runtime add/remove of lower layers ("dynamic layers"),
behaving similarly to AUFS driver.

New mount options: maxlayers=<n> enables the feature; on remount,
lowerdir+=<path> adds a read-only layer at the top of the stack, and
lowerdir-=<path> removes one (fails with -EBUSY if still in use). This
lets PorteuX/Porteus/Slax-style systems activate and deactivate .xzm
squashfs modules on a running root filesystem without a reboot - the
one feature these distros needed from AUFS. New file:
fs/overlayfs/dynlayer.c.

